---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Kilnbook for schools and colleges"
	description="Wheel booking, kiln firing queues and classes for school and college ceramics departments with one or two kilns and a semester timetable."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">For schools &amp; colleges</p>
			<h1>A ceramics room that keeps up with the timetable.</h1>
			<p class="lede narrow">
				Wheel bookings, firing queues and classes in one place, set up around your semester. Built
				for departments with one or two kilns and a room full of students who want a wheel between
				classes.
			</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-alt">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">How it fits</p>
			<h2>Three things a ceramics department juggles</h2>
			<div class="cards">
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Wheels between classes</h3>
					<p>
						Students reserve wheels, hand-building tables and the slab roller in one-hour blocks.
						You decide how many hours they get each week and how far ahead they can book, so a free
						period is not a race for the good wheel.
					</p>
					<a href="/features/wheel-time">Wheel and table booking</a>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>One or two kilns, one queue each</h3>
					<p>
						Students log a piece from their phone when it goes on the shelf. Each kiln has its own
						bisque and glaze queue, every firing is logged with the date, cone and who loaded it,
						and students get a text when their work is ready.
					</p>
					<a href="/features/firings">How firing queues work</a>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Classes on a semester timetable</h3>
					<p>
						Set up each course as a fixed series of sessions and let students book their seat.
						Instructors get their own login with the roster and can mark attendance from the studio
						tablet.
					</p>
					<a href="/features/classes">Classes and packs</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Which plan fits a department?</h2>
		<p>
			The Studio plan covers up to 3 kilns with unlimited members, so a department with one or two
			kilns has room to add another. It includes wheel and table reservations, class waitlists and
			pickup texts when pieces come out of the kiln. <a href="/pricing">Compare plans</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Questions departments ask</h2>
		<div class="faq">
			<details>
				<summary>Do schools get a discount?</summary>
				<p>
					Yes. School ceramics programs and registered nonprofits get 30% off any plan. Mention it
					when you book a demo.
				</p>
			</details>
			<details>
				<summary>Can we import our class lists?</summary>
				<p>
					Yes. Upload a CSV with names and emails, and we map the columns for you during setup.
				</p>
			</details>
			<details>
				<summary>What if we add a fourth kiln?</summary>
				<p>
					The Studio plan covers up to 3 kilns. You can move to Collective, which has no kiln limit,
					at any point in the month. We prorate the difference on your next invoice.
				</p>
			</details>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>Get your ceramics room off the sign-up sheet.</h2>
			<p>30 days free on the Studio plan. No card to start, and nothing is deleted if you walk away.</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
